  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type/png",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Portable Network Graphics"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Portable Network Graphics"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "PNG – Portable Network Graphics – es un formato de archivo de gráficos rasterizados que admite compresión de datos sin pérdida. PNG fue creado como un reemplazo mejorado y no patentado del formato GIF (Graphics Interchange Format), y es el formato de compresión de imagen sin pérdida más utilizado en Internet."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PNG – Portable Network Graphics – is a raster graphics file format that supports lossless data compression. PNG was created as an improved, non-patented replacement for Graphics Interchange Format (GIF), and is the most widely used lossless image compression format on the Internet."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/image/png"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/PNG"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": ".png"
      },
      {
        "@value": "image/png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "PNG"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PNG"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type/ogcapi_tiles",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Servicio OGC API Tiles"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "OGC API Tiles service"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "OGC API – Tiles es un estándar del Open Geospatial Consortium que define una API RESTful para acceder a datos geoespaciales en forma de teselas predefinidas. Soporta tanto teselas de mapas rasterizados como teselas vectoriales. Reemplaza al estándar WMTS anterior, utilizando principios modernos de la web."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "OGC API – Tiles is an Open Geospatial Consortium standard that defines a RESTful API for accessing geospatial data in the form of predefined tiles. It supports both raster map tiles and vector tiles. It replaces the older WMTS standard, using modern web principles."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": "image/png; image/jpeg; application/vnd.mapbox-vector-tile"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "OGC API Tiles"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "OGC API Tiles"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type/xhtml5",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Extensible Hypertext Markup Language 5"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Extensible Hypertext Markup Language 5"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Los documentos XML deben servirse con un tipo de medio Internet XML (frecuentemente llamado 'tipo MIME') como application/xhtml+xml o application/xml, y deben cumplir con la sintaxis estricta y bien formada de XML. XHTML 5 es simplemente datos HTML 5 serializados como XML, enviados con uno de los tipos de medio XML. El HTML escrito para conformar tanto las especificaciones HTML como XHTML se conoce como marcado políglota. No existe DTD para XHTML5."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "XML documents must be served with an XML Internet media type (often called ‘MIME type’) such as application/xhtml+xml or application/xml, and must conform to strict, well-formed syntax of XML. XHTML 5 is simply XML-serialized HTML 5 data (that is, HTML 5 constrained to XHTML’s strict requirements, e.g., not having any unclosed tags), sent with one of XML media types. HTML that has been written to conform to both the HTML and XHTML specifications and therefore produces the same DOM tree whether parsed as HTML or XML is known as polyglot markup. There is no DTD for XHTML5."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/application/xhtml+xml"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XHTML5"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation": [
      {
        "@value": ".html; .htm; .xhtml; .xht"
      },
      {
        "@value": "application/xhtml+xml"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
